llama.cpp patch: per-request activation capture and additive steering for llama-server
=====================================================================================

Base: ggml-org/llama.cpp commit 9a286ac98d2cab74231bd3f1fc3f2b8bdf05422e
      ("docs: improve Windows build instructions (#27381)", 2026-08-21).
Apply: git checkout 9a286ac98d2cab74231bd3f1fc3f2b8bdf05422e && git apply llama-cpp-capture-activations.patch
It may need small manual fixes on later upstream revisions (server files change often).

Adds to tools/server (see patches/README.md for the API):
  * activation_capture.h — an eval callback on the per-layer residual output ("l_out-N" /
    "final_output-N"): live per-layer means (GET/POST /activations), per-token collection to a
    binary file (POST /activations/collect, optional FFN-intermediate tensor), projection
    write-back steering and additive steering (POST /activations/steer), and per-request
    accumulation of the mean residual vector over a completion's decoded tokens.
  * /completion fields: capture_activations, capture_skip, capture_layers -> the final result
    carries "activation_means". Requires -np 1; refused under speculative decoding.
  * src/llama-context.cpp: set the eval callback on every ubatch (also when a graph is reused).
  * LLAMA_NO_ACTIVATION_CAPTURE=1 disables the callback registration entirely.

Everything is off by default; with capture disabled the callback declines every tensor.
The endpoints are unauthenticated and /activations/collect and /activations/steer read or write
server-side file paths: bind the server to 127.0.0.1.

